    historyContent: {
      origins: "NLK is a Hungarian card game learned from students at Szeged University. The initials stand for an obscene Hungarian phrase: N=nagy (big), L=any nationality starting with L (litvÃ¡n, lengyel, luxemburgi), K=kibaszÃ³s (roughly 'screwing'). The game is light-hearted and best with about six players.",
