        rules: {
          objective: 'Avoid being the last player holding cards at the end of Phase Two.',
          gameplay: "Two phases. Phase One: take turns anticlockwise; draw the top card of the talon and place it on your stack, and optionally give away cards from your stack or drawn talon cards onto opponents' stacks when a card fits (next rank above; lowest rank fits on Ace). Phase Two: play in tricks; beat the previous card with a higher card of the same suit or a trump, or pick up the lowest card in the trick. Last player left holding cards loses.",
          keyRules: [
            'Phase One: accumulate cards, give away cards that fit (next rank higher)',
            "Phase Two: shed cards by beating; pick up lowest if can't beat",
            'Lowest rank fits on Ace (wrap-around)',
            'No obligation to follow suit in Phase Twoâ€”just must beat or pick up',
            'Trumps determined by last talon card drawn',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "In Phase One, try to accumulate a small stack by giving away cards whenever possible. Cards that fit on opponents' stacks are your friends.",
          intermediate: "Plan your Phase Two hand during Phase One. Keep track of which cards you've seen. The trump suit is unknown until the last talon cardâ€”plan for flexibility.",
          advanced: "In Phase Two, sometimes picking up a low card is better than using a high card to beat. Save your high cards for when you really need them. Force opponents to pick up by playing cards they can't easily beat.",
          tips: [
            'In Phase One, Aces are dangerous because only the lowest rank can fit on them',
            "Watch the talon sizeâ€”when it's low, prepare for Phase Two",
            'Picking up the lowest card in a trick can be strategic if it gives you a useful card',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
